---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PartnerBadges from '../../components/PartnerBadges.astro';

const faqs = [
  { question: 'Does a citation in an AI answer mean my page ranks first?', answer: 'No. Bing Webmaster Tools AI Performance reports citation activity across supported AI experiences. Microsoft says those counts do not indicate ranking, authority or placement in an answer.' },
  { question: 'Does Search Console report sales from AI features?', answer: 'No. Google describes its generative AI reports as visibility reporting for URLs shown in AI features in Search and Discover. Sales need a separate business and analytics readout.' },
  { question: 'Does the GA4 AI Assistant channel show every AI-influenced visit?', answer: 'No. Google assigns the channel when a referrer matches a recognised AI assistant. Visits without that matching referral and later effects are outside that channel count.' }
];
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    { '@type': 'Article', headline: 'Ads in the Age of AI Summaries', description: 'A guide to paid placements, organic links, citations and the current reporting limits of AI search.', url: 'https://visible-ads.com/blog/ads-in-the-age-of-ai-summaries', datePublished: '2025-05-15', dateModified: '2026-10-04', author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Visible Ads', url: 'https://visible-ads.com' }, publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Visible Ads', url: 'https://visible-ads.com' }, image: 'https://visible-ads.com/images/visible-ads-og.png' },
    { '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map(({ question, answer }) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: question, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: answer } })) },
    { '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://visible-ads.com/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://visible-ads.com/blog' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Ads in AI Summaries', item: 'https://visible-ads.com/blog/ads-in-the-age-of-ai-summaries' }] }
  ]
};
---

<Layout title="Ads in the Age of AI Summaries | Visible Ads" description="Separate paid placements, organic links and citations in AI search, then read each reporting tool within its limits." schema={schema}>
  <section class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-gradient-to-br from-navy to-navy-light relative overflow-hidden" data-animate><div class="absolute inset-0 dot-pattern opacity-5"></div><div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative"><nav class="text-sm text-slate-light mb-8"><a href="/" class="hover:text-white">Home</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><a href="/blog/" class="hover:text-white">Blog</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><span class="text-white">AI summaries</span></nav><div class="max-w-3xl"><span class="inline-block px-4 py-1.5 bg-electric/20 text-electric-light text-sm font-medium rounded-full mb-6">AI search measurement</span><h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-heading font-extrabold text-white leading-tight mb-6">Ads in the age of AI summaries</h1><p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-slate-light leading-relaxed">An ad, an organic link and a citation can appear around an AI answer. Each has a different owner, reporting method and commercial meaning.</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-6">Three appearances to record separately</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed"><strong>Paid placements</strong> are advertising inventory governed by a platform's campaign, auction, eligibility and policy rules. Microsoft documents ads within Copilot responses for specific eligible campaign and ad types. OpenAI says ChatGPT ads are clearly labelled, separate from answers and shown to eligible users on supported plans. A placement requires platform approval and delivery; being eligible does not promise either.</p><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed"><strong>Organic links</strong> are links to pages surfaced as part of an unpaid search experience. They can produce a visit when someone clicks through. Their visibility depends on the search product, page and query, not on a media purchase.</p><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Citations</strong> identify source material referenced by a generated answer. A citation may be visible even when the reader does not visit the source. A citation count is therefore a visibility measure. It does not show an ad impression, a search ranking or a sale. Keep these three categories separate in the report and in the budget discussion.</p></div></section>

  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-sky-tint" data-animate><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-8">What each reporting tool measures</h2><div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><caption class="sr-only">AI search reporting tools and limits</caption><thead class="bg-navy text-white"><tr><th scope="col" class="p-4">Tool</th><th scope="col" class="p-4">Current signal</th><th scope="col" class="p-4">What it cannot establish</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-700"><tr class="border-t"><th scope="row" class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">Bing Webmaster Tools AI Performance</th><td class="p-4">Citation counts, cited pages, grounding query samples and trends across supported AI experiences.</td><td class="p-4">Ranking, authority, exact placement or a commercial result.</td></tr><tr class="border-t bg-sky-tint/40"><th scope="row" class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">Google Search Console</th><td class="p-4">URL impressions in generative AI features in Search and Discover, with page and country views.</td><td class="p-4">Paid delivery or a conversion caused by an AI feature.</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><th scope="row" class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">Google Analytics AI Assistant channel</th><td class="p-4">Visits whose referrer matches a recognised AI assistant.</td><td class="p-4">All AI influence, including visits with no matching referrer.</td></tr><tr class="border-t bg-sky-tint/40"><th scope="row" class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">Ad platform reporting</th><td class="p-4">The platform's campaign delivery and attributed outcomes where available.</td><td class="p-4">Incremental sales by itself. Microsoft currently has no Copilot-specific ad metrics.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>

  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-6">Bing citations and Copilot ads answer different questions</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">Microsoft introduced AI Performance in Bing Webmaster Tools as a public preview in February 2026. It covers citations across Microsoft Copilot, AI-generated Bing summaries and selected partner experiences. The report identifies cited pages and samples grounding queries. Microsoft explicitly says citation counts do not indicate ranking or placement within an answer.</p><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">The <a href="/bing-ads/" class="text-electric underline">Microsoft Ads service page</a> explains paid Copilot eligibility and the campaign checks needed to assess it. Microsoft says eligible ad types are automatically opted in, yet there is no guaranteed display and no current Copilot-specific ad metric. Keep Webmaster citations and paid campaign results in separate columns. Neither tells you the site's share of all possible AI answers.</p><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Our <a href="/blog/chatgpt-ads/" class="text-electric underline">ChatGPT ads guide</a> covers UK advertiser access and a controlled test. ChatGPT's labelled ads are also separate from citations or product results in an answer.</p></div></section>

  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-sky-tint" data-animate><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-8">A sensible monthly review</h2><div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6"><div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-3">Visibility</h3><p class="text-gray-700">Track cited URLs and Search Console AI impressions by page and country. Mark which product supplied each signal.</p></div><div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-3">Visits</h3><p class="text-gray-700">Review recognised AI assistant referrals and organic landing pages. Record gaps in referrer and tracking coverage.</p></div><div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-3">Business outcome</h3><p class="text-gray-700">Reconcile leads or orders with campaign costs and contribution. Use a defined test before crediting a budget change with growth.</p></div></div><p class="mt-8 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The <a href="/blog/multi-channel-attribution/" class="text-electric underline">attribution guide</a> sets out a reporting and test process. Our <a href="/multi-channel-services/" class="text-electric underline">multi-channel service</a> connects those decisions with active campaigns. Visibility trends are worth reviewing, but an ad budget should follow measured commercial outcomes.</p></div></section>

  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-8">Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="space-y-4">{faqs.map((faq) => <details class="group border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-heading font-semibold text-navy">{faq.question}</summary><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">{faq.answer}</p></details>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="py-10 bg-sky-tint"><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-4">Sources</h2><ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li><a href="https://blogs.bing.com/webmaster/2026/2/Introducing-AI-Performance-in-Bing-Webmaster-Tools-Public-Preview/" class="text-electric underline">Bing Webmaster Blog: AI Performance</a>, citation metrics and their limits.</li><li><a href="https://developers.google.com/search/blog/2026/06/gen-ai-performance-reports" class="text-electric underline">Google Search Central: generative AI performance reports</a>, Search and Discover visibility scope.</li><li><a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/9164320" class="text-electric underline">Google Analytics release notes</a>, recognised AI assistant referrals.</li><li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/advertising/msa-help/hlp_ba_conc_adsforcopilot" class="text-electric underline">Microsoft Advertising: Ads in Copilot</a>, eligibility and reporting limits.</li><li><a href="https://help.openai.com/en-us/articles/20001047-ads-in-chatgpt" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: Ads in ChatGPT</a>, labels, placement and eligibility.</li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="py-12 bg-sky-tint border-y border-gray-100" data-animate><div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><PartnerBadges compact /></div></section>
  <section class="relative py-20 lg:py-28 bg-navy" data-animate><div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center"><h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-white mb-6">Review paid search with clearer evidence</h2><p class="text-lg text-slate-light mb-8">Check the campaigns, conversion definitions and business outcomes together.</p><a href="/free-ads-audit/" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center bg-cta text-white font-semibold px-10 py-4 rounded-xl hover:bg-electric transition-colors text-lg">Get your free ads audit</a></div></section>
</Layout>
